# Packaging artefacts (Epic K3b): the herdr plugin and the
# agent skill ship in the sdist alongside the engine, so the
# documented `herdr plugin link` route works from an unpacked
# sdist as well as from a clone.
graft herdr-plugin-codereview
graft skills
# D-003 (external Phase 0–1 report, 2026-11-06): the sdist
# must be able to run its own test suite. Ship everything the
# suite reads: the full tests tree (fixtures included), the
# probe definitions, the public benchmark corpus, the examples,
# and the top-level data/docs files tests and tooling load.
# bench/ as a whole is NOT grafted — only bench/corpus; the
# registered run material (sealed sets, generation caches,
# confirmation records) stays out of the distribution.
graft tests
graft probes
graft bench/corpus
graft examples
include CHANGELOG.md precedents.json fixtures-manifest.json THREAT-MODEL.md
# 0.13.1: the PyPI landing page (pyproject readme) ships in the sdist.
include PYPI-README.md
# D-003 closure (2026-11-06): the first widening still left 12
# unpacked-suite errors, all traced to three more bench reads —
# the generation machinery module (test_generation,
# test_generation_driver, test_error_persistence), the bench
# scripts incl. the confirmation scorer (test_score_confirmation_v3
# and the generation driver; the scripts dir holds code and
# scripted-seat fixtures only — no seals, sets, or outputs), and
# the baseline doc the claim lint guards (test_claim_lint).
# Single bench files are included individually; bench/ as a
# whole is still NOT grafted, and the sealed/registered trees
# (bench/sealed, bench/generation-v2, bench/generation-v3,
# bench/confirmation-b2) stay out of the distribution.
include bench/generation.py bench/BASELINE-2026-11-04.md
graft bench/scripts
# Same closure, second layer (the import fixes unmasked three
# deeper reads): the panel configs the v3 scorer's family map
# loads (bench/configs — five small JSONs: panel configs and
# scripted-seat fixtures), the shipped v1 baseline results the
# legacy-record test loads (single file), and the expanded-clean
# stratum the registered v2 scorer loads whole via
# load_expanded_clean() (manifest + every case's case.json and
# diff.patch). expanded-clean is attempt-1's CONSUMED clean
# stratum — post-run, A1-adjudicated dev data, not a sealed or
# live registered set; the sealed/live trees (bench/sealed,
# bench/generation-v2, bench/generation-v3,
# bench/confirmation-b2) remain excluded.
graft bench/configs
graft bench/expanded-clean
include bench/baseline-2026-11-04-results.jsonl
# P6-14 (external Phase 6 rerun, 2026-11-06): the claim
# lint guards every shipped reader-facing doc, and its
# scope test asserts the set — the bench claims sheet and
# public benchmark, the pilot kit's four docs, and the
# root roadmap / review notes were not in the sdist, so
# the unpacked suite failed exactly that test and the
# distribution's lint silently guarded a smaller set than
# a clone's. Ship them (the D-003 principle: the sdist
# carries everything its own suite reads). pilot/demo is
# NOT included — it is a record tree, out of the lint's
# scope and out of the distribution.
include bench/CLAIMS-SHEET.md bench/PUBLIC-BENCHMARK.md
include pilot/QUICKSTART.md pilot/SECURITY-AND-DATA.md
include pilot/DEMO.md pilot/FEEDBACK-FORM.md
include ROADMAP.md REVIEW-NOTES.md
